## DESCRIPTION
## Find the percentage of a soft-drink flavor preference from a table.
## ENDDESCRIPTION
## DBsubject(Arithmetic)
## DBchapter(Percents)
## DBsection(Applications)
## KEYWORDS('percent', 'soda', 'soft drink')
## MLT(percents_from_table5)
## Level(1)
## MO(1)

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');
Context("LimitedNumeric");
$a   = random(46, 60);
$b   = random(21, 33, 2);
$c   = 120 - $a - $b;
$d   = random(37, 43);
$e   = random(18, 23);
$f   = random(18, 29);
$sum = $a + $b + $c + $d + $e + $f;
$p   = 1000 * $b;
$pp  = $p % $sum;
$r   = 2 * $pp < $sum ? 0 : 1;
$ans = Real((($p - $pp) / $sum + $r) / 10);
$fa  = 10000 * $b % $sum;
$fb  = (10000 * $b - $fa) / (100 * $sum);
BEGIN_PGML
A group of people are asked their soft drink preferences. The results are
listed in a table:

[#
    [.Flavor of Soft Drink.][.Number of People.]{headerrow => 1}*
    [. Cola .] [. [$a] .]*
    [. Orange .] [. [$b] .]*
    [. Lemon Lime .] [. [$c] .]*
    [. Root Beer .] [. [$d] .]*
    [. Cherry .] [. [$e] .]*
    [. Grape .] [. [$f] .]*
#]

The percent of of those who prefer orange soda is [_]{$ans}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
There are [`[$a]+[$b]+[$c]+[$d]+[$e]+[$f] =[$sum]`] people of whom [$b] prefer orange soda.


 Thus the fraction that prefer orange soda is [``\frac{[$b]}{[$sum]}``].   
To convert this fraction to a percent we multiply by 100 and perform the division 

[```\frac{100*[$b]}{[$sum]}=[$fb]```]

which, rounded to one decimal place is [$ans].
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
